    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are prioritizing high-leverage opportunities today, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (76.16) and **Jacob Wilson** (74.08), our two strongest plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a rare alignment of factors against Peralta; his efficiency is bolstered by a favorable matchup and a slow SP delivery, which significantly enhances his stolen base probability in our scarcity-focused model. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** leverages a massive +10% park factor boost and a soft matchup against Bradford, making him a critical engine for today's run production. **Jackson Merrill** also provides elite value (69.57) against Bibee, benefiting from a +13% dynamic platoon edge that keeps his start firmly in the \"Strong\" territory despite a challenging opponent.\n\nStrategic benching remains a high-stakes balancing act as we protect game caps. **Miguel Vargas** (44.43) was the most difficult exclusion, narrowly missing the cut behind **Dominic Smith** and **Heliot Ramos**. While **Miguel Vargas** showcased strong xwOBA metrics, the optimizer favored the positional utility and higher base-scoring floor of our active starters. We are also closely monitoring the pending status of **Wade Meckler** and **Andy Pages**; while both projected as starts, their scores are sensitive to actual lineup placement. **Andy Pages** faces a significant hurdle today against the elite arm of Logan Henderson, as does **Kyle Tucker**, whose score is suppressed by the same difficult matchup, necessitating careful observation once lineups are finalized. \n\nBeyond these matchups, we are navigating a high-risk environment with several hitters facing elite arms. The presence of Cease on the mound creates a distinct disadvantage for **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** and **Heliot Ramos**, whose efficiency scores are heavily dragged down by a -19% SP skill penalty. While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** maintains a respectable 56.52 score due to his leadoff-adjacent spot, **Heliot Ramos** sits right on the borderline at 45.00. We will continue to monitor weather and late scratch news, as any further degradation in conditions could force a pivot to our bench depth, including **Coby Mayo**, should we need to abandon our more aggressive projections against tough pitching.",
